    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection as specified, keeping structural impact low: **3 files touched**, one new small class, and only `static` helper methods changed (each `service` orchestration method left untouched).\n\n**`Soundex.java` (new)** \u2014 a small, cohesive utility (`code` + a private `digit` lookup) producing the American Soundex code of a surname. Shared by both the identity key and the soft-match, so the phonetic logic lives in one place.\n\n**`CheckUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 rewrote only the static `identityKey(owner)` helper (plus three tiny private helpers) so the key is now `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`. The `service` method (the 409 gate) is unchanged, so it still ignores deleted owners and self, and the POST pipeline still runs the email-domain blocklist (`CheckEmailDomain`) before it. The mapper's `identityKey` expression needed no change since the signature is preserved \u2014 the response now exposes the 64-hex key.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 the soft match now fires when `identityKey` differs but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match (dropping the old normalized-lastName + different-telephone check and the now-unused `equalsTelephone` helper).\n\nBehavioural consequences, all satisfied:\n- Telephone is part of the key, so two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** are no longer a hard duplicate \u2014 they're created and flagged as a soft match.\n- The former household-duplicate 409 (`CheckUniqueHousehold`) was already not wired into `owners.POST.yml`; identity is now the single duplicate gate, and `householdId` no longer participates in the key (it's still assigned for tier/ceiling rules).\n\n`AcceptanceTest` (both tests \u2014 64-hex key shape and identical-identity \u2192 409) passes; `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
